{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines","id":1524720,"title":"What is ACTUALLY stronger: Abilities and Attributes, or Disciplines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-29T17:36:58-07:00","id":1524720,"title":"What is ACTUALLY stronger: Abilities and Attributes, or Disciplines?","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I was talking to some friends and I noticed that we seem to understand very differently some of the rules of the VtM20 and VDA20. I'd be interested to hear people's views.<br /> <br /> Some might have seen some other post about intimidation and werewolves, so that is what sparked the discussion between us. We got into discussing how intimidation works in general (not just with lupines) and social rolls at large, though it could be applied to all abilities. <br /> <br /> When I read, say, VDA20, I see that social rolls have quite well defined mechanics and results. Also non-social rolls, like the Stealth rolls to sneak. Many are contrasted rolls with a given difficulty that can be adjusted to suit the circumstances. The winner in the contrasted rolls does what they wanted to do or foil the other's attempt. Spending Willpower can add one success to your roll and prevent botches.<br /> By contrast, a disicpline like Presence is both stronger and weaker: it is stronger because it can do something that's very hard to do with contrasted rolls with a single non-contrasted roll at a given difficulty; it is weaker because it is enough to spend 1 willpower point and roll Willpower at diff.8 to be protected from the emotions stirred by the Discipline. Dominate allows you to utter commands subtly and implant them with single rolls whereas normal intimidation gets others to do what you want (they become cowed, i.e. they submit to your wish, as per the Oxford Languages definition of the term) but after a contrasted roll and in a rather plainly threatening way, likely to draw attention and enmity and a bad reputation. But you can resist Dominate if you're good at not looking in the eyes. Animalism 3 also makes people cowed in a special sense, likely more intense than the one for simple intimidation. It grants an easier roll at a fixed difficulty with which you may cow even the strongest mind. Obfuscate and the Stealth ability are similar: you can do a lot of things unnoticed with a good Stealth rating, but Obfuscate allows you to do the same without needing to roll,but might be shattered by things that you could avoid by activele using Stealth. .<br /> My understanding therefore is that disciplines do not replace or compete with standard interaction, but occupy a different space to it. And standard interaction has a truer nature than the false emotions produced by Presence, hence why people can resist the latter by spending Willpower, but not so much the former. After intimidation, opponents are &quot;effectively cowed&quot;, as the book says, and it is regardless of the supernatural nature of the victims: they already have higher Willpower and Strength and Intimiidate ratings as supernaturals, so why should they get an extra vague bonus that is not in the books if one interacts with them without using disciplines?<br /> My friends seem convinced that normal abilities do nothing except against some human, and that anything supernatural needs to go through disciplines to be defined and effective, and that, since Presence can be dismissed with 1 point of Willpower, social interactions must be weaker than that - though this is not written anywhere in the book and I think it missed the point of Presence altogether.<br /> <br /> A look at the description of what is commonly done with each level of each ability in the manual would also support the idea that abilities are already capable of geting done many things without powers.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T19:14:40-07:00","id":1524724,"title":"","content":"Disciplines often have a greater effect but typically require grounding in Attributes and Abilities; if you have low or nonexistence Stealth, you won't be getting much out of Obfuscate. If you don't put any work into social Abilities, your Presence probably won't work too well. It's not quite like Charms for the Exalted, but it's close enough to make the question kind of a weird one to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T19:41:43-07:00","id":1524728,"title":"","content":"To do my best, I guess, to give a functional answer: they're generally tied (though specific exceptions exist).<br /> <br /> Abilities are the most efficient of the three, but have the lowest &quot;cap&quot; in how much they can accomplish; even if that can be in breadth instead of depth.<br /> <br /> Attributes are in the middle. They cost more than Abilities, and do more than Abilities.<br /> <br /> Disciplines aren't efficient in the sense of having high individual costs, and requiring decent investments in other traits to get solid use out of them. But they can expand character capabilities beyond what Abilities and Attributes can do on their own.<br /> <br /> People frequently treat the last part of how Disciplines expand your PC's potential, as what makes them stronger, but you can look at plenty of theory craft threads about different &quot;builds&quot; and see that this is simply because high Abilities and Attributes (or things like Generation for high vitae cost ones, and Willpower for Thaumaturgy) are just assumed to have been invested in first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T19:45:10-07:00","id":1524729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524724#post1524724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines often have a greater effect but typically require grounding in Attributes and Abilities; if you have low or nonexistence Stealth, you won't be getting much out of Obfuscate. If you don't put any work into social Abilities, your Presence probably won't work too well. It's not quite like Charms for the Exalted, but it's close enough to make the question kind of a weird one to ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 mean, the question opening the thread is deliberately provocative. Obviously disciplines allow one to do what abilities allow and much more.<br /> <br /> My main problem is not with the attributes and abilities themselves, but with the standard actions one can do with them before even thinking of doing disciplines. My friends seem to think those standard actions are just minor things against humans, despite the core manual giving examples of them being used betweem vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T21:06:33-07:00","id":1524733,"title":"","content":"In general you'd be much better off with 5 dots of Charisma and 5 dots of Leadership or Intimidation and no dots in Presence than you would be with 5 dots of Presence but with 1 dot in Charisma and no dots Leadership or Intimidation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T00:23:19-07:00","id":1524739,"title":"","content":"Your friends expectations are out of step with the rules. It's completely viable to play VtM in such fashion, but the actual rules aren't going to work well with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T05:55:44-07:00","id":1524754,"title":"","content":"all three must work in concert to be truly powerful, admittedly there are exceptions, Potence is more powerful than raw Strength, but it is cheaper to improve your Strength than your Potence (unless it is a Clan Discipline).<br /> <br /> but almost all Discipline abilities that do not rely on Attributes or Abilities will cost you (often Heavily) in Blood and/or Willpower, both finite resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28255-dropbear","name":"DropBear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T10:49:39-07:00","id":1524761,"title":"","content":"I always went with the notion that having the proper skills was more important then followed by raw attributes with the disciplines last as it lays the groundwork for making a good and potent character and not to mention what is your general idea of what said character is.<br /> <br /> IE a Kindred who likes to meet new people should have good social skills and attributes before of thinking of learning Presence as they might use it poorly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T13:05:29-07:00","id":1524766,"title":"","content":"Indeed, skills and attributes are way more usefull and effective - not to mention used more in a Chronicle - than the Disciplines<br /> For example, regarding &quot;Torture&quot;, mentions the Sabbat Tzimisce Priest Stefan Kostas who still speaks with great pride of how he extracted vital military information from a Gangrel Archon, using nothing but a 50 cent disposable razor, three needles, a pack of Holiday Inn matches, a rubber tube and a gallon of Clorox.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:08:54-07:00","id":1524809,"title":"","content":"Dramatic Actions taken with Attribute + Ability are powerful but - tipically - mundane. They won't allow you to do the literally impossible, nor are they mandated to work if what you're asking for it's absurd.<br /> <br /> The way I understand it: With Dramatic Rules, after you declare what you want to do and how, the ST it's the one in charge of deciding what Atribute + Skill you're going to use, at what Diff, and how many successes ...<i> or if the roll it's possible at all.</i><br /> <br /> To give some examples:<br /> <br /> *If you were surrounded by a group of enemies, you can't climb the tree next to you and become &quot;functionally hidden in plain sight&quot;, the way Obfuscate 4 does, with just rolling Stealth and a trillon successes &quot;at Diff 10. Because it's absurd&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's how the system it's intended to work. You would have to <i>sell me your &quot;misdirection&quot;</i> in a way that it's at least somewhat credible, <i>then </i>I would determine things like Diff, and so, and so.<br /> <br /> <i>In that sense</i>, Obfuscate it's more &quot;powerful&quot; than Stealth. Which doesn't mean it's more important for a Stealth build, considering all it's weaknesses and that you will have to have Stealth anyway<br /> <br /> *I would say you can't &quot;cow&quot; a sept of werewolves into worshipping Set by whiping your tail against the ground and yelling very hard &quot;convert or die!&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is not about &quot;Werewolves being immune to Intimidation because they're too cool for that shit&quot;, it's about an action that doesn't seem it would realisticlly be followed by that conclussion, to a point it goes beyond what Diff 10. it's supposed to represent in the way how I see it.<br /> <br /> If you had a Discipline that does just that, barring other powers countering it, it would work. Because &quot;it's magic&quot;. In *that* sense, it could be considered &quot;more p\u00f2werful&quot; <hr /><br /> Maybe the difference I'm trying to express could be summarized as that you don't get to explain things as &quot;a wizard did it&quot; if you're using mundane skills, so the result depends much more on the criteria of the ST about how the world works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:25:31-07:00","id":1524812,"title":"","content":"Disciplines can useful tools for sure, but if you don't have any real intelligence to use it properly then you are going to in heaps of trouble like Aleph example of using Obfuscate to hide in a tree when the baddies have a good sight line on you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:24:22-07:00","id":1524838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524809#post1524809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dramatic Actions taken with Attribute + Ability are powerful but - tipically - mundane. They won't allow you to do the literally impossible, nor are they mandated to work if what you're asking for it's absurd.<br /> <br /> The way I understand it: With Dramatic Rules, after you declare what you want to do and how, the ST it's the one in charge of deciding what Atribute + Skill you're going to use, at what Diff, and how many successes ...<i> or if the roll it's possible at all.</i><br /> <br /> To give some examples:<br /> <br /> *If you were surrounded by a group of enemies, you can't climb the tree next to you and become &quot;functionally hidden in plain sight&quot;, the way Obfuscate 4 does, with just rolling Stealth and a trillon successes &quot;at Diff 10. Because it's absurd&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's how the system it's intended to work. You would have to <i>sell me your &quot;misdirection&quot;</i> in a way that it's at least somewhat credible, <i>then </i>I would determine things like Diff, and so, and so.<br /> <br /> <i>In that sense</i>, Obfuscate it's more &quot;powerful&quot; than Stealth. Which doesn't mean it's more important for a Stealth build, considering all it's weaknesses and that you will have to have Stealth anyway<br /> <br /> *I would say you can't &quot;cow&quot; a sept of werewolves into worshipping Set by whiping your tail against the ground and yelling very hard &quot;convert or die!&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is not about &quot;Werewolves being immune to Intimidation because they're too cool for that shit&quot;, it's about an action that doesn't seem it would realisticlly be followed by that conclussion, to a point it goes beyond what Diff 10. it's supposed to represent in the way how I see it.<br /> <br /> If you had a Discipline that does just that, barring other powers countering it, it would work. Because &quot;it's magic&quot;. In *that* sense, it could be considered &quot;more p\u00f2werful&quot; <hr /><br /> Maybe the difference I'm trying to express could be summarized as that you don't get to explain things as &quot;a wizard did it&quot; if you're using mundane skills, so the result depends much more on the criteria of the ST about how the world works.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, thank you. You actually gave me an idea on how to set difficulties for rolls using as reference the descriptions of what each Attribute and Ability can do on each dot. It would need adjustment due to many factors, but I might try something like 4 + the amount of dots fitting the description of what you're trying to do (similar to some forms of Blood Magic). For example, in VDA20 the description of Stealth for dots 4 and 5 is:<br /> 4: Expert: You could tweak your target\u2019s noses if you wanted, and disappear again before they blinked.<br /> 5: Master: You were never there. No one ever saw you. You\u2019ve infiltrated fortified keeps and sat in on the most secret of meetings. Your name is spoken in awe by highwaymen and in consternation by lawkeepers.<br /> <br /> So if a player said they wanted to tweak a target's nose and disappear before they blinked (for example by swiftly going behind their back and staying out of their line of sight right behind them until they manage to leave unseen, movie like but not actually magical), I would give them difficulty 8. If they wanted to infiltrate a fortified keep and sit in the most secret of meetings, it would be difficulty 9. Obviously it would be a contrasted roll against the opponents' relevant traits, thus rolling a single success would not typically cut it.<br /> A more complex way of doing this would be to look at the Attribute dot that does a comparable thing, and the Ability dot, and add them together. Ex.: if what you're trying to do seems to fit the description for Dexterity 3 combined with that of Stealth 4, your difficulty is 7. Just an idea. Still need to mull it over. And needs adjustment, as I said.<br /> <br /> Second, I see what you mean with the examples and the wizard thing.<br /> <br /> Third, as specified in the other thread, the intention was not to convert. It was your standard medieval fantasy &quot;surrender to my god or die&quot; supported by a display of strength (12 + 5 activated Potence, which is way more than 5 dots in Strength) superior to most things they deal with (which cap at Strength 10, regardless of their other powers) plus 2 powers amplifying my intimidation and a Road bearing relevant to conversions and appearing divine (houserules with the ST because the Road had no specified bearing in the VDA20 manual). The reason why genuine conversion was discussed in the thread was because I wasn't sure how to interpret scoring 7 successes more than the opponents on a roll like this, because it's supposed to be well above and beyond what I intended or hoped to achieve. I just hoped for a faked submission, small lowering of the head and ceasing hostility as long as I vacated the premises swiftly, but 7 successes (mathematically averaged against a Garou maxed in Strength and Intimidation, not some lucky roll) should have some dramatic weight and also indicate that the character's level of perceived menace (even though in reality he's not that mighty) is way above the normal levels of interactions between werewolf and vampire stats.<br /> If you have a Road bearing specific to conversions and appearing divine, both of which are almost miraculous things generally, and that bearing is -3, taking every difficulty 10 task to a merely challenging difficulty 7, I would be cool with ruling that it can do, with a mundane roll, pretty over the top things. <br /> I would say the same if a characted had the VDA20 Road of Bones at 10 and the merit Powerful Aura, granting him -3 difficulty on any Stealth roll. His limits are definitely not those of others when it comes to Stealth. I count Road bearings as a supernatural, mystical benefit, and they do expand the scope of what is normally possible for a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 10-31-2023, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T12:05:12-07:00","id":1524876,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it the Road of Set? I would think that having a potent aura for that road would be less than stellar for convincing Garou of anything but &quot;I'm worth a lot of Glory!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T15:13:43-07:00","id":1524888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524766#post1524766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, skills and attributes are way more usefull and effective - not to mention used more in a Chronicle - than the Disciplines<br /> For example, regarding &quot;Torture&quot;, mentions the Sabbat Tzimisce Priest Stefan Kostas who still speaks with great pride of how he extracted vital military information from a Gangrel Archon, using nothing but a 50 cent disposable razor, three needles, a pack of Holiday Inn matches, a rubber tube and a gallon of Clorox.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Add in some bad music from really bad singers and you probably get people to spill anything for it to stop.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll tell you everything you want to know, Stop with the Steven Seagal songs!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T16:47:27-07:00","id":1524891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524876#post1524876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't it the Road of Set? I would think that having a potent aura for that road would be less than stellar for convincing Garou of anything but &quot;I'm worth a lot of Glory!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 mean, that's just not how Road aura works, tbh... Especially in as far as it reflects how much you have tamed the Beast, even on a path whose values are sort of Wyrmish... Especially in that time and edition, Road of Set could mean &quot;Set is good and wants to save the world from otherworldly horrors and to do so he took the powers of his arch-enemy Apep and the burden and bad rep that come with them and we're commanded to keep corrupting so we can keep his cover up, so nobody realises he's saving the world from evils the rest of the Ennead refused to acknowledge.&quot; But, yeah, it's a secret thing anyway. To Garou \u0130 guess we just smell more of Wyrm because of corrupting a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T06:31:10-07:00","id":1524911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524838#post1524838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, thank you. You actually gave me an idea on how to set difficulties for rolls using as reference the descriptions of what each Attribute and Ability can do on each dot...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't do that. The descriptions aren't rules, they're flavor. They can be used to adjudicate stuff, but more as a sort of &quot;inspiration&quot; than actual guidelines. The levels 4 and 5 are intended to &quot;amaze&quot; w/o actually taking in count what would be needed to make the feat<br /> <br /> This is very evident when you've seen the skills trough editions. Their &quot;potency&quot;, if you want to call it that, it's wildly different for no reason. And sometimes set expectations that aren't very consistent with the RAW.<br /> Like, there was one edition where Brawl 5 said you can knock out 3 persons in one move - by the rules of combat that would involve a lot more than just Brawl 5. A lot of the descriptors are &quot;you're this famous person&quot;, neglecting that such a person wouldn't only have a dicepool of that Skill, but also much more varied Skills and Backrounds that allow to do those feats of investigation or criminality<br /> <br /> My understanding of the RAW, it's that it's intended to be arbitrary. This may not be satisfying from the pov of a player, but the whole point of the ST system it's to give a lot of leeway to the ST. You will see that's constantly stress out trough the rules.<br /> <br /> TLDR, I don't think any ST it's mandated, or even encouraged, to allow someone with just Stealth to become invisible while figthing &quot;at Dif 8&quot; (T<i>hat could actually be better than Obfuscate 4 at doing what Obfuscate 4 does, depending on circumnstances, and would be magick in all but name</i>. Which it's patently not how the RAI works, in particular because it's the work of the ST to decide how &quot;cinematic&quot; they want to roll)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-02-2023, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T07:32:30-07:00","id":1524916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524838#post1524838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4: Expert: You could tweak your target\u2019s noses if you wanted, and disappear again before they blinked.<br /> 5: Master: You were never there. No one ever saw you. You\u2019ve infiltrated fortified keeps and sat in on the most secret of meetings. Your name is spoken in awe by highwaymen and in consternation by lawkeepers.<br /> <br /> So if a player said they wanted to tweak a target's nose and disappear before they blinked (for example by swiftly going behind their back and staying out of their line of sight right behind them until they manage to leave unseen, movie like but not actually magical), I would give them difficulty 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've written a post about how, in general, one shouldn't take those descriptions to heart because they're fluff, but it was flagged.<br /> <br /> I wanna add that, I think, what that lvl 4 it's trying to say it's not that you can easily vanish from the very sigth of the target at Skill level 4, but rather that if you were already hidden, you could do something of the like w/o being immediately blown out. It says &quot;disappear <b>again</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know, like the comedy routine where a guy claps another guy, and that guy instead blames a third one because that one was closer, and/or the first hid very fast. Manipulation + Stealth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ? <br /> <br /> *Hidding behind back of moving guy <i>who knows you're there</i> <u>until you can leave unseen</u> sounds beyond that description to me, and frankly more cartoonish than cinematic. I woudln't allow it at diff 10, let alone 8<br /> <br /> Most ST's out there will refuse to treat your average Skills as &quot;superpowers&quot;. That's what Disciplines are for.<br /> <br /> If people it's arguing Skills aren't, in fact, &quot;less powerful&quot;, it's because a lot can be attained w/o such &quot;superpowers&quot;, perhaps even more so. Assuredly more so than with those supperpowers being badly used.<br /> <br /> Of course Skills are useful against Vampires, Werewolves, and whatnot - heck, im pretty sure Vampire says that using Disciplines on other vampires on an Elyseum it's very poor etiquete, even if the use was allowed in the first place. So, <i>obviously </i>they work on vampires<br /> <br /> ... but not as the heavy sledgehammer that's I see implied in that example and others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T08:19:45-07:00","id":1524920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524916#post1524916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most ST's out there will refuse to treat your average Skills as &quot;superpowers&quot;. That's what Disciplines are for.<br /> <br /> If people it's arguing Skills aren't, in fact, &quot;less powerful&quot;, it's because a lot can be attained w/o such &quot;superpowers&quot;, perhaps even more so. Assuredly more so than with those supperpowers being badly used.<br /> <br /> Of course Skills are useful against Vampires, Werewolves, and whatnot - heck, im pretty sure Vampire says that using Disciplines on other vampires on an Elyseum it's very poor etiquete, even if the use was allowed in the first place. So, <i>obviously </i>they work on vampires<br /> <br /> ... but not as the heavy sledgehammer that's I see implied in that example and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Skills are not superpowers, \u0130 agree. \u0130 do think, however, that if a character - PC or NPC - has supernatural bonuses to rolls for mundane skills, he can do things that are normally impossible but still within the purview of that skill. Some things lower difficulties, which to me already means that the difficult becomes easy; the absurd, challenging; the impossible, absurd and therefore attemptable - if still conceivable somehow in the situation. Some characters have traits above 5, which also means that they are beyond the limits we are familiar with in the real world, at least to a degree. \u0130n fact, having traits above 5 is itself a supernatural thing, a power of sorts. \u0130 factor that in if \u0130 need to assess what can or cannot be done with a roll. Especially since traits above 5 and strong Road bearing modifiers are themselves things rarer in the game than disciplines at levels 1-5, so \u0130 think they deserve accurate representation. A character with a Dexterity + Stealth dice pool beyond 10 is inhumanly swift and able to avoid doing what humans typically notice. He will still need to do contrasted rolls - while an Obfuscate user can ignore the roll altogether - but as long as he scores more successes than his opponents at a given difficulty, \u0130 have no issue imagining them vanishing unnoticed. Or if a character has 10 dots in the Road of Bones with Powerful Aura and has therefore -3 difficulty to Stealth rolls, \u0130 consider them supernaturally enhanced for such rolls and will allow things that \u0130 would otherwise class as difficulty 11,12 or 13, for which they would roll at 8,9 and 10 respectively.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T08:23:33-07:00","id":1524921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524720-what-is-actually-stronger-abilities-and-attributes-or-disciplines?p=1524916#post1524916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I've written a post about how, in general, one shouldn't take those descriptions to heart because they're fluff, but it was flagged.<br /> <br /> I wanna add that, I think, what that lvl 4 it's trying to say it's not that you can easily vanish from the very sigth of the target at Skill level 4, but rather that if you were already hidden, you could do something of the like w/o being immediately blown out. It says &quot;disappear <b>again</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know, like the comedy routine where a guy claps another guy, and that guy instead blames a third one because that one was closer, and/or the first hid very fast. Manipulation + Stealth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?<br /> <br /> *Hidding behind back of moving guy <i>who knows you're there</i> <u>until you can leave unseen</u> sounds beyond that description to me, and frankly more cartoonish than cinematic. I woudln't allow it at diff 10, let alone 8<br /> <br /> Most ST's out there will refuse to treat your average Skills as &quot;superpowers&quot;. That's what Disciplines are for.<br /> <br /> If people it's arguing Skills aren't, in fact, &quot;less powerful&quot;, it's because a lot can be attained w/o such &quot;superpowers&quot;, perhaps even more so. Assuredly more so than with those supperpowers being badly used.<br /> <br /> Of course Skills are useful against Vampires, Werewolves, and whatnot - heck, im pretty sure Vampire says that using Disciplines on other vampires on an Elyseum it's very poor etiquete, even if the use was allowed in the first place. So, <i>obviously </i>they work on vampires<br /> <br /> ... but not as the heavy sledgehammer that's I see implied in that example and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 agree that the descriptions are fluff, but they are still all we have to get an idea, and they are meant to exemplify certain levels of human ability - and humans cen be amazing sometimes.<br /> \u0130f Empathy 5 says that you can read what is in people's hearts, \u0130 don't take it to mean that you have a cheaper version of Auspex 4, but rather that through observing people, your understanding of human nature and circumstances is such that you can take extremely good guesses consistently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}